# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Settings for the Aisle demo box.
#
#  ⚠️ THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE. Every value is blank on purpose.
#
#  This repository is public, so no real password, key or connection string is ever
#  committed to it. The working version of this file is delivered separately, alongside
#  the submission, as `aisle.env`.
#
#  TO RUN THE BOX:
#    1. Copy the delivered `aisle.env` into this folder and rename it to `.env`
#       (the leading dot matters — Docker Compose looks for exactly that name).
#    2. Open it and fill in GEMINI_API_KEY. That is the only line you need to touch.
#    3. Run `docker compose up --build` from this folder.
#
#  You do NOT need to copy this template. It exists so the shape of the settings is
#  visible in the repository without any secret being in it.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── The one line you fill in yourself ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The AI agent talks to Google's Gemini model, and Google requires a key that identifies
# who is calling. Free keys take about two minutes to create at https://aistudio.google.com
#
# You can leave this blank. Everything else in Aisle still works — browsing products,
# editing them, adjusting stock, signing in. Only the AI chat panel is switched off.
GEMINI_API_KEY=


# ── The database ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Where the product and conversation data lives. A "connection string" is one line that
# bundles the database's address, name, username and password together, so nothing here
# ever prompts you to log in to a database.
#
# Delivered filled in. Do not edit.
DATABASE_URL=


# ── The login server's own applications ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The login server needs to recognise the website and the AI agent as things it has met
# before. Each of them therefore has an ID (like a name badge) and a secret (like the
# signature that proves the badge is really theirs).
#
# These belong to THIS BOX ONLY. They are not the developer's own credentials, and they
# are useless anywhere except against the copy of the login server running on your own
# machine.
#
# Delivered filled in. Do not edit.
AISLE_GATE_CLIENT_ID=
AISLE_GATE_CLIENT_SECRET=
AISLE_AGENT_CLIENT_ID=
AISLE_AGENT_CLIENT_SECRET=

# The key the website uses to seal its own session cookie, so the browser cannot tamper
# with it. Delivered filled in. Do not edit.
THUNDERID_SECRET=
